# Dynamic & Interactive — Kiddy Link

## Golden rule
Every user-visible **business data** and every **button/action** must be real: loaded from API/DB and wired to working behavior. No placeholders, no silent controls.

## No static business content
- Lists, counts, labels, banners, calendar events, stickers, homework, photos, messages, notifications → **from API/DB only**
- Never hardcode arrays of students, teachers, parents, stickers, levels, or menu data that should live in MySQL
- Backend: seed/sample data in `prisma/seed.ts` only — runtime reads/writes via Prisma
- Flutter: fetch via `ApiClient` / repositories; show loading → data → empty/error states

```dart
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded list
final items = ['رحلة', 'إجازة', 'اجتماع'];

// ✅ GOOD
final items = await contentRepository.getCalendarEvents();
```

## No silent / dead buttons
- Every `ElevatedButton`, `ListTile`, `IconButton`, menu tile **must** have a working `onPressed` / `onTap`
- Forbidden: empty callbacks, `null` handlers, tiles with subtitle "API/Swagger only", commented-out navigation
- If feature is not built yet → **do not show the button**; or implement the screen + API first

```dart
// ❌ BAD
_MenuTile(title: 'إدارة المعلمات', onTap: () {}),

// ✅ GOOD — full flow or hidden until ready
_MenuTile(
  title: 'إدارة المعلمات',
  onTap: () => Navigator.push(context, MaterialPageRoute(
    builder: (_) => const AdminTeachersScreen(),
  )),
),
```

## Interactive UX (required)
- All forms: validate → API call → success/error feedback (`SnackBar` / inline error)
- Lists: pull-to-refresh or reload after mutations
- Loading: `CircularProgressIndicator` while fetching; disable submit while `isLoading`
- Empty state: clear Arabic message when API returns `[]`
- Errors: show user-friendly Arabic message, never fail silently

## Backend coupling
- New Flutter screen → matching NestJS module + Prisma model/migration if needed
- No mock data in production paths; no `Future.delayed` fake responses
- CRUD must persist to MySQL and reflect on next GET

## Fixed UI chrome (allowed)
- Short labels for actions ("تسجيل الدخول", "حفظ", "إلغاء") may live in widgets or a single `app_strings.dart` / l10n file
- Theme, colors, icons — see `BRAND_IDENTITY.md`
- Business copy (banner body, event title, sticker name) → **never** hardcoded in UI

## Before finishing any task, verify
1. No new hardcoded business lists or dummy JSON in Flutter/backend
2. Every new button navigates or calls API
3. Data round-trip: UI → API → DB → UI
